    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d232">

                <pb facs="0365" n="359" sameAs="frus:frus1901China/pg359"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-01-30"><hi rendition="#italic">January 30,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Conger reports that the powers will certainly establish permanent legation
                    guards and militarily occupy points between Peking and the sea until final
                    settlement. The scheme submitted by Waldersee, which contemplates an
                    international force of from 10,000 to 12,000 men, is likely to meet general
                    approval. Prestige and interests of the United States demand that they should
                    participate.</p>
                <p>Mr. Conger asks what reply he shall make.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
